                <pb facs="0276" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.5151/1754: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-11T12:00:00+00:00">March 11,
                        1938—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 11—8:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>371. The Paris editor of the <hi rendition="#italic">New York Herald
                    Tribune</hi>, commenting upon the report that Blum had acceded to the Radical
                    Socialist demand <pb facs="0277" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> for rejection of
                    exchange control, added that “a reliable source said last night pressure from
                    the Treasury Department in Washington had helped him to make up his mind”.</p>
                <p>We have received inquiries regarding this story and have replied that it is
                    absurd.</p>
                <p>There is no mention of the story in the French press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
